{
  "file": "module4",
  "page": 159,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        67.39069366455078,
        527.5992431640625,
        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "As with any other TB medicine and regimen, safety precautions are required to ensure the rapid",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        80.59070587158203,
        527.5069580078125,
        95.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "identification and proper management of any serious adverse event. Close clinical monitoring is",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        93.79071807861328,
        527.4508056640625,
        108.23371887207031
      ],
      "text": "essential for all patients receiving this regimen, particularly liver function tests, given the hepatotoxic",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        106.99073028564453,
        527.420166015625,
        121.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "potential of prolonged pyrazinamide use. If possible, all patients should be tested each month for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        120.19074249267578,
        527.3881225585938,
        134.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "levels of AST (also known as serum glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase, SGOT). If resources are not",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        133.3907012939453,
        527.4156494140625,
        147.8336944580078
      ],
      "text": "available to monitor all patients on the Hr-TB treatment regimen, monthly monitoring of patients",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        146.59071350097656,
        527.61572265625,
        161.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "at high risk (e.g. patients coinfected with viral hepatitis or with a history of heavy alcohol use) is",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        159.7907257080078,
        527.3936157226562,
        174.2337188720703
      ],
      "text": "strongly advised. Additionally, to prevent and manage the potential toxic effects of ethambutol in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        172.99073791503906,
        527.403564453125,
        187.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "children (e.g. retrobulbar neuritis), it is necessary to adhere to the correct doses recommended for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        186.1907501220703,
        527.2815551757812,
        200.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "paediatric populations. Early signs of ethambutol toxicity can be tested in older children through",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        199.3907012939453,
        527.4103393554688,
        213.8336944580078
      ],
      "text": "red–green colour discrimination. Monitoring for retrobulbar neuritis can be undertaken early when",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        211.31471252441406,
        150.32960510253906,
        227.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "(117) appropriate  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        241.02191162109375,
        466.6474914550781,
        265.8169250488281
      ],
      "text": "5. Monitoring and management strategies for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 19.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        263.8218994140625,
        268.1544494628906,
        288.6169128417969
      ],
      "text": "MDR/RR-TB treatment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 19.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        294.06793212890625,
        527.4256591796875,
        308.5109558105469
      ],
      "text": "People who receive MDR/RR-TB regimens need to be monitored during treatment using relevant",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        307.267822265625,
        527.4255981445312,
        321.7108459472656
      ],
      "text": "clinical and laboratory testing schedules. Response to treatment and toxicity are monitored through",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        320.4678039550781,
        527.4666748046875,
        334.91082763671875
      ],
      "text": "regular history taking, physical examination and CXR; special tests (e.g. audiometry, visual acuity tests,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.979631423950195,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        333.6678161621094,
        527.4849853515625,
        348.11083984375
      ],
      "text": "peripheral neurological examination and electrocardiography); and laboratory monitoring. Using",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        346.8677978515625,
        527.4376831054688,
        361.3108215332031
      ],
      "text": "smear microscopy or culture to assess the conversion of bacteriological status is an important way",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        360.06781005859375,
        208.81707763671875,
        374.5108337402344
      ],
      "text": "to assess treatment response.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        381.7716979980469,
        527.2244262695312,
        396.2147216796875
      ],
      "text": "NTPs should aim for complete registration of patients with MDR/RR-TB through follow-up and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        394.9717102050781,
        527.4234008789062,
        409.41473388671875
      ],
      "text": "monitoring of treatment outcomes as part of national surveillance. Regular review of MDR/RR-TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        408.17169189453125,
        527.446533203125,
        422.6147155761719
      ],
      "text": "cohort data is essential. The prospective collection of accurate data for key variables at the case-based",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.966299057006836,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        421.3717041015625,
        527.3992919921875,
        435.8147277832031
      ],
      "text": "level, using an electronic register, is strongly advised, both for the benefit of the individual patient,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        434.57171630859375,
        306.0242004394531,
        449.0147399902344
      ],
      "text": "and to inform revisions of local and global policies.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        456.27569580078125,
        527.4486694335938,
        470.7187194824219
      ],
      "text": "The WHO framework for aDSM needs to be applied to patients on any type of MDR/RR-TB regimen,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        469.4757080078125,
        527.4290771484375,
        483.9187316894531
      ],
      "text": "to ensure appropriate action and an acceptable level of monitoring for AEs and prompt response",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        482.67572021484375,
        527.3276977539062,
        497.1187438964844
      ],
      "text": "to such events, alongside monitoring for treatment outcomes. The rationale for aDSM is largely",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        495.8757019042969,
        527.4322509765625,
        510.3187255859375
      ],
      "text": "supported by the increasing use worldwide of combinations of new and repurposed medications in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        509.0755615234375,
        527.4235229492188,
        523.5185546875
      ],
      "text": "MDR/RR-TB treatment regimens. Additional evidence generated on AEs will be important to build",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        522.2756958007812,
        398.4615783691406,
        536.7186889648438
      ],
      "text": "the evidence base on the safety of the new regimens in varied settings.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        543.9796142578125,
        527.0653076171875,
        558.422607421875
      ],
      "text": "Access to reliable DST for bedaquiline, linezolid and all medicines composing the regimen is essential",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.98884391784668,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        557.1795654296875,
        527.4290161132812,
        571.62255859375
      ],
      "text": "to investigate reasons for lack of bacteriological and clinical improvement – in an ideal situation, the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        570.379638671875,
        527.5335693359375,
        584.8226318359375
      ],
      "text": "DST for all second-line medicines used in regimens would be available. This should not, however, delay",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.958271026611328,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        583.57958984375,
        527.1297607421875,
        598.0225830078125
      ],
      "text": "the initiation of life-saving treatment. Before starting a 9-month regimen, the patient’s bacteriological",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.989395141601562,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        596.7796020507812,
        527.5596313476562,
        611.2225952148438
      ],
      "text": "status should be available, with confirmation of TB disease, MDR/RR-TB (as a minimum) and FQ",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        609.9796142578125,
        527.406005859375,
        624.422607421875
      ],
      "text": "susceptibility. Country programmes need to strengthen and increase access to FQ DST and undertake",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.973518371582031,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        623.1796264648438,
        527.428955078125,
        637.6226196289062
      ],
      "text": "surveillance for emerging drug resistance, including for bedaquiline and all second-line medicines",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        636.379638671875,
        527.4445190429688,
        650.8226318359375
      ],
      "text": "for which reliable DST is available. The FQ DST is also important to support the prescription of the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        649.57958984375,
        527.4442138671875,
        664.0225830078125
      ],
      "text": "relevant combination of 6-month regimens – BPaLM, BPaL, BDLLfxC, BDLLfx or BDLC – to maximize",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        662.7796020507812,
        527.389404296875,
        677.2225952148438
      ],
      "text": "efficacy and prevent unnecessary potential toxicity. The need for FQ DST should not be a barrier to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        675.9796142578125,
        527.4022827148438,
        690.422607421875
      ],
      "text": "starting treatment with 6-month regimens, because each regimen has a combination that can be",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        689.1796264648438,
        312.78033447265625,
        703.6226196289062
      ],
      "text": "started even though the FQ DST is not yet available.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        710.8834838867188,
        527.5394287109375,
        725.3264770507812
      ],
      "text": "Country programmes are also strongly encouraged to establish the DST capacity to test for resistance",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.977777481079102,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        724.0836181640625,
        527.4002685546875,
        738.526611328125
      ],
      "text": "to bedaquiline and linezolid at baseline (particularly in cases demonstrating FQ resistance), and to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        737.2835083007812,
        527.620849609375,
        751.7265014648438
      ],
      "text": "test samples from patients with no bacteriological conversion after 4 months or recurrences while on",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.998099327087402,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        750.4835205078125,
        527.450927734375,
        764.926513671875
      ],
      "text": "the 6-month regimens. The implementation of 9-month regimens requires the use of routine DST to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        330.23760986328125,
        801.0170288085938,
        556.099609375,
        811.52099609375
      ],
      "text": "Chapter 2 Drug-resistant TB treatment: Recommendations  145",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "heading"
    }
  ]
}